WEBVTT

00:00.307 --> 00:02.385
- Scarlett and Hansol's teacher gave them

00:02.385 --> 00:04.369
a system of linear equations to solve.

00:04.369 --> 00:05.922
They each took a few steps that lead

00:05.922 --> 00:07.825
to the systems shown in the table below.

00:07.825 --> 00:08.788
So this is the teacher system.

00:08.788 --> 00:11.308
This is what Scarlett got
after taking some steps.

00:11.308 --> 00:12.909
This is what Hansol got.

00:12.909 --> 00:14.106
Which of them obtained a system

00:14.106 --> 00:17.019
that is equivalent to
the teacher's system?

00:17.019 --> 00:17.681
And just to remind ourselves,

00:17.681 --> 00:19.701
an equivalent system is a system

00:19.701 --> 00:21.303
that has, or at least for our purposes,

00:21.303 --> 00:23.822
is a system that has the same solution,

00:23.822 --> 00:25.320
or the same solution set.

00:25.320 --> 00:26.898
So if there is a certain xy

00:26.898 --> 00:28.268
that satisfies this system

00:28.268 --> 00:31.160
in order for Scarlett's
system to be equivalent

00:31.160 --> 00:33.458
it needs to have the same solution.

00:33.458 --> 00:34.967
So let's look at this.

00:34.967 --> 00:36.406
So Scarlett, let's see,

00:36.406 --> 00:39.159
let's see if we can match these up.

00:39.159 --> 00:43.465
So her second equation here,

00:43.465 --> 00:45.473
so this is interesting,

00:45.473 --> 00:49.235
her second equation 14x - 7y = 2

00:49.235 --> 00:50.813
over here the teacher has an equation

00:50.813 --> 00:54.133
14x - 7y = 7.

00:54.133 --> 00:56.745
So this is interesting because the ratio

00:56.745 --> 00:59.334
between x and y is the same,

00:59.334 --> 01:01.354
but then your constant term,

01:01.354 --> 01:04.744
the constant term is
going to be different.

01:04.744 --> 01:06.114
And I would make the claim

01:06.114 --> 01:09.109
that this alone tells you
that Scarlett's system

01:09.109 --> 01:11.629
is not equivalent to the teacher.

01:11.629 --> 01:14.624
And you're saying, well,
how can I say that?

01:14.624 --> 01:16.690
Well, these two equations if you were

01:16.690 --> 01:19.128
to write them into slope intercept form,

01:19.128 --> 01:20.590
you would see because the ratio

01:20.590 --> 01:23.895
between x and y, the x
and y terms is the same.

01:23.895 --> 01:25.637
You're going to have the same slope,

01:25.637 --> 01:27.273
but you're going to have
different Y intercepts.

01:27.273 --> 01:28.690
In fact, we can actually solve for that.

01:28.690 --> 01:30.072
So this equation right over here

01:30.072 --> 01:32.927
we can write it as if we, let's see,

01:32.927 --> 01:35.133
if we subtract 14x from both sides

01:35.133 --> 01:38.761
you get -7y - 14,

01:38.761 --> 01:41.721
woops, -7y =,

01:41.721 --> 01:45.892
is equal to -14x + 7

01:45.892 --> 01:47.749
and we could divide both sides by -7.

01:47.749 --> 01:52.485
You get y = 2x -1 so that's this...

01:52.485 --> 01:54.321
All I did is algebraically
manipulate this.

01:54.321 --> 01:55.643
This is this line and I could even try

01:55.643 --> 01:58.046
to graph it so let's do that.

01:58.046 --> 02:00.484
So I'll draw a quick coordinate.

02:00.484 --> 02:02.087
This is just going to be very rough.

02:02.087 --> 02:04.084
Quick coordinate axis right over there,

02:04.084 --> 02:06.138
and then this line,

02:06.138 --> 02:08.901
this line would look something like this.

02:08.901 --> 02:12.457
So its y intercept is -1
and it has a slope of 2.

02:12.457 --> 02:16.196
So let me draw a line with a slope of,

02:16.196 --> 02:19.071
a line with a slope of 2 might look

02:19.071 --> 02:22.493
something like that.

02:22.493 --> 02:24.935
So that's this line right over here

02:24.935 --> 02:28.499
or this one right over there,

02:28.499 --> 02:29.753
and let's see.

02:29.753 --> 02:32.992
This one over here is going to be,

02:32.992 --> 02:35.058
if we do the same algebra,

02:35.058 --> 02:36.296
we're going to have

02:36.296 --> 02:41.156
- 7y = -14x + 2,

02:41.809 --> 02:45.028
or y = , I'm just
dividing everything by -7,

02:45.028 --> 02:49.423
2x - 2/7

02:50.173 --> 02:52.018
so this is going to look
something like this.

02:52.018 --> 02:56.522
Its y intercept is -2/7 so
it's like right over there.

02:56.522 --> 02:59.401
So this line is going
to look something like,

02:59.401 --> 03:00.377
I'm going to draw my best,

03:00.377 --> 03:02.791
my best attempt at drawing it,

03:02.791 --> 03:05.257
it's going to look something...

03:05.257 --> 03:07.294
Actually that's not quite right.

03:07.294 --> 03:08.462
It's going to look something like...

03:08.462 --> 03:10.551
I'll actually just start
it right over here.

03:10.551 --> 03:13.082
It's going to look something like,

03:13.082 --> 03:14.592
something like this.

03:14.592 --> 03:16.228
It's going to have the same slope,

03:16.228 --> 03:18.608
and obviously it goes in
this direction as well.

03:18.608 --> 03:20.686
Actually, let me just draw that.

03:20.686 --> 03:22.706
So it's going to have the same slope,

03:22.706 --> 03:25.643
but at different y intercepts.

03:25.643 --> 03:27.744
That doesn't look right,
but you get the idea.

03:27.744 --> 03:29.509
These two lines are parallel.

03:29.509 --> 03:30.507
So these two lines are parallel

03:30.507 --> 03:33.386
so any coordinate that satisfies this one

03:33.386 --> 03:34.942
is not going to satisfy this one.

03:34.942 --> 03:36.868
They have no points in common.

03:36.868 --> 03:37.786
They are parallel.

03:37.786 --> 03:40.166
That's the definition of parallel.

03:40.166 --> 03:43.567
Since this and this have
no points in common,

03:43.567 --> 03:45.448
there's no way that some solution set

03:45.448 --> 03:47.503
that satisfies this would satisfy this

03:47.503 --> 03:49.964
'cause any xy that satisfies this

03:49.964 --> 03:52.448
can't satisfy this or vice versa.

03:52.448 --> 03:53.249
They're parallel.

03:53.249 --> 03:54.364
There are no points.

03:54.364 --> 03:56.824
These two things will never intersect.

03:56.824 --> 04:00.006
So Scarlett does not have
an equivalent system.

04:00.006 --> 04:02.502
Now what about Hansol?

04:02.502 --> 04:04.104
Well, we see Hansol has the same thing

04:04.104 --> 04:05.346
going on here.

04:05.346 --> 04:09.688
5x - y, 5x - y, but then the constant term

04:09.688 --> 04:13.101
is different, -6, positive 3.

04:13.101 --> 04:16.502
So this and this also
represent parallel lines.

04:16.502 --> 04:19.091
Any xy pair that satisfies this,

04:19.091 --> 04:21.204
there's no way that it's
going to satisfy this.

04:21.204 --> 04:23.003
These two lines don't intersect.

04:23.003 --> 04:24.489
They are parallel.

04:24.489 --> 04:28.651
So Hansol's system is
not equivalent either.
